WEBVTT

00:11:58.121 --> 00:12:01.662
And I think I start everything desperately
,

00:12:01.662 --> 00:12:03.579
and I think they probably all end that

00:12:03.579 --> 00:12:04.871
way, too. I love that.

00:12:05.412 --> 00:12:09.829
I want to ask you, because your
book is all about rethinking.

00:12:09.829 --> 00:12:11.871
I was just curious, do you
feel like there is

00:12:11.871 --> 00:12:16.621
a fundamental barrier to
rethinking and if so,

00:12:16.621 --> 00:12:18.579
what it is and I do have a follow up.

00:12:18.912 --> 00:12:20.662
Yeah, I think so. So, yeah,

00:12:21.079 --> 00:12:26.246
I feel like one of the things that
I've rethought twice now

00:12:26.246 --> 00:12:29.204
as I've been writing books is, you know,
I wrote my first book,

00:12:29.204 --> 00:12:32.412
Give and Take with with a whole framework
to organize the world in terms of givers,